NAME
       demo - exercise every roffsub element

SYNOPSIS
       demo [-r] [-k list] [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
       demo reads each file in turn, or the standard input when none is named, and writes the records it finds in the
       order chosen by the options. A space written as a backslash space, as in a b c, never breaks. Fonts may change
       mid word, as in srt(1) and file.txt.

       A second paragraph follows the first after one blank line, and it is long enough to wrap at every width the
       reference outputs use, which is the point of it.

OPTIONS
       -r     reverse the emitted order.

       -k list
              sort by the columns in list, then the remaining columns in order.

       --respect-blanks
              treat each indented block as a unit; the tag is longer than the indent, so the body starts on the next
              line.

       -x  a width of four sets the prevailing indent, which the next item keeps.

       -o file
           write to file instead of the standard output.

   Lists
       o      bullets use the bullet character, shown as o on an ASCII terminal.

       o      a second bullet item.

       1.  a numbered item with its own width.

       2.  a second numbered item.

   Nesting
       Text before a nested block.
              Nested text sits one prevailing indent further in.
                 A deeper block, moved in by three cells.
              Back at the first level.
       Back at the section margin.
       After a line break, still the same paragraph.


       After two blank lines.

TABLE
        OPTION   MEANING
       --------+-------------------
        -r       reverse the order
        -k KEY   sort on KEY

       A boxed table with a text block:
       -------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------
        NAME    DESCRIPTION                                                                               SIZE
       -------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------
        alpha   a long description that has to wrap when the terminal is narrow, kept inside its column     12
        beta    short                                                                                     3456
       -------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------

EXAMPLES
       demo -k5,3 file
       demo -r < input > output

SEE ALSO
       srt(1), roffsub(7)
